+## Inbound email
+
+Action Mailbox accepts raw `message/rfc822` messages at `/rails/action_mailbox/relay/inbound_emails` using the relay ingress. Authenticate with HTTP Basic credentials using username `actionmailbox` and `RAILS_INBOUND_EMAIL_PASSWORD`; configure the SMTP relay to forward the full message to this endpoint over HTTPS.
+
+A business's plain support address is its account subdomain at `HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN`. For example, Acme receives new requests at `acme@support.example.test`. A ticket's authenticated API representation includes a private ticket-specific `reply_address`; staff replies to email-origin tickets use that address as `Reply-To`, allowing the requester to continue the conversation from their mail client. Test routing runs inline and does not require a worker.
